.TH DEBRUN 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
debrun \- install a Debian package downloaded from the website of its maker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B debrun
[\fIFILE\fB.deb\fR]
.br
.B debrun
\fB--version\fR | \fB--help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBDebrun\fR is the installer of Debian packages (\fI.deb\fR files) of the
Selviana Desktop Environment. Makers of software (web browsers, editors,
chat programs) often offer their programs as a \fI.deb\fR file on their
website. Liria and the desktop open such files with Debrun (a double-click,
or \fBOpen With\fR and \fBInstall with Debrun\fR in the context menu); it is
not shown in the Start menu or the Control Center.
.PP
Before anything is installed, Debrun shows:
.IP \(bu 2
the application (its icon and name from the package's launcher), the
package name, version, architecture, maintainer, homepage, sizes and the
SHA-256 digest of the file;
.IP \(bu 2
that the package does not come from the package sources of the system, so
nobody checked it, where the browser downloaded it from (when it recorded
that) and the version the package sources offer of the same package;
.IP \(bu 2
what it changes besides its files: an APT package source and signing key
(as the packages of Chrome and VS Code add), maintainer scripts run as
root, downloads made by those scripts, scheduled tasks, system services,
programs started at login, set-user-ID programs, system users, sudo and
polkit rules, device rules, kernel modules, login (PAM) configuration,
alternatives and configuration files;
.IP \(bu 2
its dependencies, each one installed, provided by another package, to be
installed from the package sources or missing, with the other packages
installed or removed with it (APT's own simulation, \fBapt-get --simulate\fR);
.IP \(bu 2
whether it is a new installation, an upgrade, the same version again or a
downgrade, and its files.
.PP
\fBInstall\fR (or \fBUpgrade\fR, \fBReinstall\fR, \fBDowngrade\fR) asks for
an administrator's password and installs the package the Debian way: APT
installs it with the packages it needs from the configured package
sources. Changes that remove other packages are confirmed first.
\fBRemove...\fR removes the installed package of the same name. The
progress is shown with the animated SDE logo.
.PP
Errors are explained: a package made for another architecture, dependencies
the package sources cannot meet (\fBRefresh Package Lists\fR downloads the
lists again), held packages, another program using the package system, too
little disk space, a damaged or incomplete download.
.SH HOW IT INSTALLS
Debrun runs as the user. Changes are made by \fB/usr/libexec/sde/debrun-helper\fR,
started with \fBpkexec\fR(1) (polkit actions \fBorg.debion.sde.debrun.install\fR,
\fB.remove\fR and \fB.refresh\fR; an administrator's password, remembered for
a few minutes). The helper opens the file with the user's rights, copies it
to \fI/var/cache/sde/debrun\fR (writable by root only), checks that the copy
has the SHA-256 digest, name, version and architecture that Debrun showed,
simulates the change again and refuses removals that were not shown, then
runs \fBapt-get install\fR on the copy. Every request is logged to the
system log; APT and dpkg keep their own logs in \fI/var/log/apt\fR and
\fI/var/log/dpkg.log\fR.
.PP
With \fB[debrun] backend=packagekit\fR in \fIsde.conf\fR (system defaults:
\fI/etc/xdg/sde/sde.conf\fR) Debrun uses PackageKit's \fBInstallFiles\fR
instead; \fBbackend=apt\fR forces the helper; the default \fBauto\fR takes
the helper when \fBpkexec\fR is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
print a short help and exit.
.SH KEYS
\fBEnter\fR or \fBSpace\fR press the button with the keyboard focus,
\fBEscape\fR closes Debrun (not while it installs), \fBCtrl+O\fR opens
another package, \fBF1\fR shows About Debrun.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/debrun.desktop
opens \fBapplication/vnd.debian.binary-package\fR files; it is the SDE
default for them in \fI/etc/xdg/sde-mimeapps.list\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.debion.sde.debrun.policy
the polkit actions of the helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBapt\fR(8), \fBapt-get\fR(8), \fBdpkg\fR(1), \fBpkexec\fR(1),
\fBmerkadu\fR(1), \fBsde-appimage\fR(1)
.PP
The documentation in \fI/usr/share/doc/sde/DEBRUN.md\fR.
